  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed a full two-hour set at the Old Town School of Folk Music in Chicago on May 29, 2018, following a previous show there the day before [1][2]. This audience recording, captured and transferred by LMGBTapes, documents twenty-three songs across the main set and a four-song encore [1]. The lineup includes tracks from albums such as All Eternals Deck, Bedside Recordings Vol. 1.2, and Goths, alongside several unreleased pieces [1]. Notably, the set features “Good Morning to All Vultures,” which is the first appearance of that song in the archive’s collection [1][2]. Other rare moments include “New Chevrolet In Flames” and “Song for Black Sabbath's Second North American Tour,” both of which have limited archived histories [1][2]. The band offered spoken introductions touching on themes like maximum respect, the importance of the Young Center for Immigrant Children's Rights, and personal anecdotes about Matty Bones and a contestant who beat Press Your Luck [1]. The performance concludes with encores including “Wear Black” and “The Best Ever Death Metal Band In Denton” [1]. This recording is the only available capture of this specific date, providing a complete view of the night’s musical journey [1].",
